   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the maximum\ndimension and weight limitations of certain vehicles proceeding to and from a\nportion of the New York state thruway",
    "basePrintNo": "S6332",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6332-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §385, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6332\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the maximum\ndimension and weight limitations of certain vehicles proceeding to and\nfrom a portion of the New York state thruway\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation will allow tandem trucks to use less than 2 miles of\npublic road off from Thruway Exit 257A,\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 385, paragraph 16(w) to allow tandem trucks to\nuse less than 2 miles of public road off from Thruway Exit 25-A.\n\nSection 2: Effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe conversion to cashless tolling eliminates the ability of double\ntandem trucks to utilize Exit 25-A for inbound distribution. Vehicles\npassing through the exit at higher rates of speed in both directions\nrender truckers unable to access the parking lot directly adjacent to\nExit 25-A, which is where they have traditionally unhooked the second\ntrailer of the tandem in order to comply with the VTL rules prohibiting\ntandem trucks from traversing the surrounding roads.  This scenario\nwould lead to double tandem trucks to utilize alternative routes in\norder to get their freight to distribution centers, meaning even longer\ndriving time for double tandem trucks on local roads. Additionally,\nlonger driving times would negatively impact the environment by way of\nincreased emissions.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
